From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heinemeier Hansson <david@loudthinking.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p42100-asus-zenbook-14-ux3480qa: Drop
 rising-edge lid wakeup action

x1p42100-asus-zenbook-14-ux3480qa.dts inherits switch-lid (TLMM GPIO 92,
active low) with wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED> from
x1-asus-zenbook-a14.dtsi. Armed for the rising edge only, the lid
hall-sensor IRQ glitches on CX collapse exit and wakes open-lid deep
suspend, matching the same issue fixed on the Surface Laptop 8, ASUS
Zenbook A16 and Anduril BlueChip.

Delete wakeup-event-action from switch-lid so opening a closed lid still
wakes the laptop while open-lid deep sleep stays in APSS/CXSD/AOSD/DDR.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-zenbook-14-ux3480qa.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-zenbook-14-ux3480qa.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-zenbook-14-ux3480qa.dts
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 	model = "ASUS Zenbook 14 (UX3480QA)";
 	compatible = "asus,zenbook-14-ux3480qa", "qcom,x1p42100";
 
+	gpio-keys {
+		switch-lid {
+			/delete-property/ wakeup-event-action;
+		};
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * The A14's camera indicator on TLMM 110 belongs to its MIPI camera.
 	 * This camera is USB and lights its own LED; the DSDT uses TLMM 110
